{"title":"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Feasible_Shortcuts)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Feasible Shortcuts)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Leap Day, February <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ae760d1ea10eb7a90d22087b3c7e2393d02117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, occurred on a Sunday. On what day of the week will Leap Day, February <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, occur? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8ddeef0274b7b6b2575ef4ded6da82cd7f32bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\textrm{Tuesday} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\textrm{Wednesday} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\textrm{Thursday} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\textrm{Friday} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\textrm{Saturday}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"631\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988ab73be88b10c8cbf520db5e7cb4b3c6531963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$365$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> days in a year, plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra day if there is a Leap Day, which occurs on years that are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (with a few exceptions that don't affect this problem).  \n</p><p>Therefore, the number of days between Leap Day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ae760d1ea10eb7a90d22087b3c7e2393d02117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> and Leap Day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07fe0333728372482545f25f039fecd0d3dc6ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cdot 365 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 5844$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since the days of the week repeat every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39395a3a9be034eb1e92e1e0d8b69b86b86ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5844 \\equiv -1 \\bmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />, the day of the week Leap Day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> occurs is the day of the week the day before Leap Day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ae760d1ea10eb7a90d22087b3c7e2393d02117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> occurs, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f3b13308558237c3796834b1e70d22adfb0568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\textrm{Saturday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"112\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Feasible_Shortcuts.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Feasible_Shortcuts)\">Solution 2 (Feasible Shortcuts)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Feasible Shortcuts)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since every non-leap year there is one day extra after the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> weeks, we can deduce that if we were to travel forward <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> amount of non-leap years, then the answer would be \"Sunday + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />\" days.\n</p><p>However, we also have leap-years in our pool of years traveled forward, and for every leap-year that passes, we have two extra days after the 52 weeks. So we would travel \"Sunday + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />\" days. \n</p><p>Mixing these two together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> leap years <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e2b8c77961fa450124e82c3999e61543610c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2008, 2012, 2016, 2020)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> non-leap years. We thus get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6325a9cb3dbe664487885de0ad3d7c4bc2d4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + 2\\cdot 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> \"extra days\" after Sunday. Since seven days are in a week, we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f36f7ec1e7587f3e529826a0acbd138984d39a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\bmod{7} \\equiv 6$\" width=\"105\" height=\"12\" />, and six days after Sunday is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f3b13308558237c3796834b1e70d22adfb0568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\textrm{Saturday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"112\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note how we did not require any complex or time-consuming computation, and thus it will save crucial time, especially during a test like the AMC 10.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B\">2006 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2006 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\